    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d539">

                <pb facs="0473" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/1009.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 31, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>President Zamor, wife and child, sailed last night. Charles Zamor and ministers
                    remain in French Legation. Terrific firing last night. Absolute calm in the city
                    to-day. <hi rendition="#italic">Hancock</hi> arrived this morning. Conferred
                    with commander, and under the circumstances no occasion for landing troops. The
                    city is under martial law commanded by General Redmond Polynice, Acting
                    Commandant of Arrondissement, who is the sole authority for order.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
